/**
Bindings to libcurl: HTTP and HTTPS, FTP and FTPS, SFTP and SCP, SMTP
mail, and WebSockets, for OpenXTalk.

curlxt wraps libcurl 8.22.0 (with libssh2 1.11.1 for SFTP). A request is
an integer handle: make one with <cuRequestNew>, set its headers, options
and body, then start it with <cuStart>. Either wait for it on the spot with
<cuWait> (the script pauses until it ends) or let it run in the background
and call <cuPoll> on a timer, which moves every running request along and
says which ones have finished. Read the outcome with <cuInfo>, <cuText> and
<cuBody>, then release the handle with <cuFree>. A handle that has gone
stale is a harmless no-op.

Nothing moves between calls: a background request makes progress only
while <cuPoll> or <cuWait> runs. The curlHelpers library (cuStartPolling)
runs the timer for you and sends your callback when a request ends, and the
tsNet library gives scripts written for LiveCode's tsNet external the same
calls, built on this one.

A WebSocket (ws:// or wss://) is a request handle too. Make one with
<cuWsNew>, start it with <cuStart>, and once it is open send with
<cuWsSendText> or <cuWsSendData> and read what has arrived with
<cuWsReadText> or <cuWsRead>. It moves while <cuWsPoll> (or <cuPoll>)
runs. The curlHelpers library (cuWsOpen) does all of that and sends your
handler a message for each thing that happens.

Call <cuInitialize> once at startup and <cuCleanup> once at quit.

Tags: Networking, Library
*/
library org.openxtalk.library.curl

-- curl.lcb - the LCB binding for curlxt (library org.openxtalk.library.curl).
-- It declares one `private foreign handler` per cux_* symbol in
-- src/cux_abi.h and wraps each in a `public cu*` handler. Options, info
-- fields and text fields are addressed by NAME from script ("timeout",
-- "responseCode", "headers"); the numbers live only here and in the header,
-- and tools/check-abi-registry.py proves the two never drift.
--
-- THE MODEL: PUMP OR NOTHING (as in enetxt). The shim starts no thread and
-- never calls script. A started request moves only while cuPoll or cuWait
-- runs; the helpers library runs cuPoll on a timer.
--
-- The FFI idiom for buffers is the family's (carried from enetxt, which
-- carried it from TorrentXT): output buffers are raw blocks from the engine
-- <builtin> MCMemoryAllocate passed as a Pointer; input buffers pass
-- MCDataGetBytePtr(theData) with a byte count; every foreign call sits inside
-- `unsafe ... end unsafe`; every `variable` is declared at the top of its
-- handler.
--
-- The out-buffer contract: a text call returns the bytes written, or
-- -(bytes needed) when the buffer is too small. The scratch buffer is never
-- smaller than kScratchCap, so a "needed" answer is always below
-- -kScratchCap and can never be mistaken for one of the small error codes.
--
-- Every edit gets the static gate (tools/check-livecodescript.py). Since
-- 2026-11-21 the native lane also compiles this file with OXT-Beyond's own
-- lc-compile -Werror and RUNS tests/engine-selftest.lc on that release's
-- headless server engine (Linux x86-64), which calls every public handler;
-- the IDE and the other platforms need an OXT pass.

use com.livecode.foreign

metadata version is "0.2.0"
metadata author is "Seth Morrow Software"
metadata title is "curlxt"

-- Android gives a process no socket without the INTERNET permission. OXT's
-- standalone builder reads this key from every extension an app includes
-- and writes the permission into the app's manifest, so including this
-- library is enough; no other platform reads it. Added 2026-11-18;
-- verified statically; needs an OXT pass on Android.
metadata android.permissions is "INTERNET"

-- ===================================================================== --
--  Constants (mirror src/cux_abi.h; tools/check-abi-registry.py)
-- ===================================================================== --

-- Must equal CUX_ABI_VERSION in src/cux_abi.h; _checkABI() throws on skew.
constant kABIVersion is 2

-- kMCStringEncodingUTF8, the engine's own enum value.
constant kEncodingUtf8 is 4

-- The reusable scratch buffer's floor (see the out-buffer contract above).
constant kScratchCap is 4096

constant kStateNew is 0
constant kStateRunning is 1
constant kStateDone is 2

constant kResultCancelled is 1000

constant kOptTimeoutMs is 1
constant kOptConnectTimeoutMs is 2
constant kOptFollowRedirects is 3
constant kOptMaxRedirects is 4
constant kOptVerifyPeer is 5
constant kOptVerifyHost is 6
constant kOptLowSpeedLimit is 7
constant kOptLowSpeedTime is 8
constant kOptUseSsl is 9
constant kOptFtpPassive is 10
constant kOptMaxBodyBytes is 11
constant kOptHttpVersion is 12
constant kOptDnsCacheSeconds is 13
constant kOptCreateDirs is 14
constant kOptWsCloseTimeoutMs is 15

constant kOptUsername is 101
constant kOptPassword is 102
constant kOptProxy is 103
constant kOptCaFile is 104
constant kOptOutputFile is 105
constant kOptInputFile is 106
constant kOptMailFrom is 107
constant kOptMailRcpt is 108
constant kOptUserAgent is 109
constant kOptSshPublicKey is 110
constant kOptSshPrivateKey is 111
constant kOptKeyPassword is 112
constant kOptQuote is 113
constant kOptPostQuote is 114
constant kOptProxyUserpwd is 115
constant kOptReferer is 116
constant kOptAcceptEncoding is 117

constant kInfoState is 1
constant kInfoResult is 2
constant kInfoResponseCode is 3
constant kInfoBytesDown is 4
constant kInfoBytesUp is 5
constant kInfoLengthDown is 6
constant kInfoLengthUp is 7
constant kInfoTotalTime is 8
constant kInfoRedirectCount is 9
constant kInfoBodySize is 10
constant kInfoCancelled is 11
constant kInfoWsState is 12
constant kInfoWsMessages is 13
constant kInfoWsNextType is 14
constant kInfoWsNextSize is 15
constant kInfoWsCloseCode is 16
constant kInfoWsQueuedBytes is 17
constant kInfoWsPongs is 18

constant kTextHeaders is 1
constant kTextError is 2
constant kTextEffectiveUrl is 3
constant kTextContentType is 4
constant kTextMethod is 5
constant kTextWsCloseReason is 6

-- WebSockets (ABI 2): the states cuInfo(h, "wsState") answers, the message
-- kinds, and the close codes the shim itself reports.
constant kWsConnecting is 1
constant kWsOpen is 2
constant kWsClosing is 3
constant kWsClosed is 4

constant kWsKindText is 1
constant kWsKindBinary is 2
constant kWsKindPing is 3
constant kWsKindPong is 4

constant kWsCodeNormal is 1000
constant kWsCodeNoStatus is 1005
constant kWsCodeAbnormal is 1006
constant kWsCodeTooBig is 1009

-- ===================================================================== --
--  Module state: the reusable scratch buffer
-- ===================================================================== --

variable sScratchPtr as Pointer
variable sScratchCap as Integer

-- ===================================================================== --
--  Foreign handlers (one per cux_* symbol in cux_abi.h). Never rename.
-- ===================================================================== --

private foreign handler _cux_abi_version() returns CInt binds to "c:curlxt>cux_abi_version!cdecl"
private foreign handler _cux_init() returns CInt binds to "c:curlxt>cux_init!cdecl"
private foreign handler _cux_cleanup() returns CInt binds to "c:curlxt>cux_cleanup!cdecl"
private foreign handler _cux_version_string(in pOut as Pointer, in pCap as CInt) returns CInt binds to "c:curlxt>cux_version_string!cdecl"
private foreign handler _cux_last_error(in pOut as Pointer, in pCap as CInt) returns CInt binds to "c:curlxt>cux_last_error!cdecl"
private foreign handler _cux_clear_error() returns nothing binds to "c:curlxt>cux_clear_error!cdecl"

private foreign handler _cux_request_new(in pMethod as ZStringUTF8, in pUrl as ZStringUTF8) returns CInt binds to "c:curlxt>cux_request_new!cdecl"
private foreign handler _cux_set_header(in pReq as CInt, in pLine as ZStringUTF8) returns CInt binds to "c:curlxt>cux_set_header!cdecl"
private foreign handler _cux_set_int(in pReq as CInt, in pOption as CInt, in pValue as CInt) returns CInt binds to "c:curlxt>cux_set_int!cdecl"
private foreign handler _cux_set_text(in pReq as CInt, in pOption as CInt, in pValue as ZStringUTF8) returns CInt binds to "c:curlxt>cux_set_text!cdecl"
private foreign handler _cux_set_body(in pReq as CInt, in pBytes as Pointer, in pLen as CInt) returns CInt binds to "c:curlxt>cux_set_body!cdecl"
private foreign handler _cux_start(in pReq as CInt) returns CInt binds to "c:curlxt>cux_start!cdecl"
private foreign handler _cux_cancel(in pReq as CInt) returns CInt binds to "c:curlxt>cux_cancel!cdecl"
private foreign handler _cux_free(in pReq as CInt) returns CInt binds to "c:curlxt>cux_free!cdecl"

private foreign handler _cux_poll(in pOut as Pointer, in pCap as CInt) returns CInt binds to "c:curlxt>cux_poll!cdecl"
private foreign handler _cux_wait(in pReq as CInt, in pTimeoutMs as CInt) returns CInt binds to "c:curlxt>cux_wait!cdecl"

private foreign handler _cux_info(in pReq as CInt, in pField as CInt) returns CDouble binds to "c:curlxt>cux_info!cdecl"
private foreign handler _cux_text(in pReq as CInt, in pField as CInt, in pOut as Pointer, in pCap as CInt) returns CInt binds to "c:curlxt>cux_text!cdecl"
private foreign handler _cux_body(in pReq as CInt, in pOut as Pointer, in pCap as CInt) returns CInt binds to "c:curlxt>cux_body!cdecl"
private foreign handler _cux_live_count() returns CInt binds to "c:curlxt>cux_live_count!cdecl"

private foreign handler _cux_ws_new(in pUrl as ZStringUTF8) returns CInt binds to "c:curlxt>cux_ws_new!cdecl"
private foreign handler _cux_ws_send(in pReq as CInt, in pKind as CInt, in pBytes as Pointer, in pLen as CInt) returns CInt binds to "c:curlxt>cux_ws_send!cdecl"
private foreign handler _cux_ws_close(in pReq as CInt, in pCode as CInt, in pReason as ZStringUTF8) returns CInt binds to "c:curlxt>cux_ws_close!cdecl"
private foreign handler _cux_ws_read(in pReq as CInt, in pOut as Pointer, in pCap as CInt) returns CInt binds to "c:curlxt>cux_ws_read!cdecl"
private foreign handler _cux_ws_poll() returns CInt binds to "c:curlxt>cux_ws_poll!cdecl"
private foreign handler _cux_ws_wait(in pReq as CInt, in pTimeoutMs as CInt) returns CInt binds to "c:curlxt>cux_ws_wait!cdecl"

-- ===================================================================== --
--  Engine Foundation <builtin> foreign handlers (resolve by NAME: no `_`)
-- ===================================================================== --
private foreign handler MCStringEncode(in pString as String, in pEncoding as CInt, in pIsExternalRep as CBool, out rData as Data) returns CBool binds to "<builtin>"
private foreign handler MCStringDecode(in pData as Data, in pEncoding as CInt, in pIsExternalRep as CBool, out rString as String) returns CBool binds to "<builtin>"
private foreign handler MCMemoryAllocate(in pSize as UIntSize, out rBlock as Pointer) returns CBool binds to "<builtin>"
private foreign handler MCMemoryDeallocate(in pBlock as Pointer) returns nothing binds to "<builtin>"
private foreign handler MCDataCreateWithBytes(in pBytes as Pointer, in pCount as CUInt, out rData as Data) returns CBool binds to "<builtin>"
private foreign handler MCDataGetBytePtr(in pData as Data) returns Pointer binds to "<builtin>"

-- ===================================================================== --
--  Private helpers
-- ===================================================================== --

-- A legible throw at startup beats a crash at first use.
private handler _checkABI()
   variable tABI as Integer
   unsafe
      put _cux_abi_version() into tABI
   end unsafe
   if tABI is not kABIVersion then
      throw "curlxt native library ABI does not match the LCB binding; rebuild and repackage the native library."
   end if
end handler

-- Grow the scratch buffer to at least pNeed bytes (never below kScratchCap).
private handler _ensureScratch(in pNeed as Integer)
   variable tOk as Boolean
   variable tWant as Integer
   put pNeed into tWant
   if tWant < kScratchCap then
      put kScratchCap into tWant
   end if
   if sScratchCap < tWant then
      if sScratchCap > 0 then
         unsafe
            MCMemoryDeallocate(sScratchPtr)
         end unsafe
      end if
      put false into tOk
      unsafe
         put MCMemoryAllocate(tWant, sScratchPtr) into tOk
      end unsafe
      if not tOk then
         put 0 into sScratchCap
         throw "curlxt: failed to allocate the scratch buffer."
      end if
      put tWant into sScratchCap
   end if
end handler

private handler _bufToData(in pPtr as Pointer, in pLen as Integer) returns Data
   variable tData as Data
   variable tOk as Boolean
   put the empty data into tData
   if pLen > 0 then
      put false into tOk
      unsafe
         put MCDataCreateWithBytes(pPtr, pLen, tData) into tOk
      end unsafe
      if not tOk then
         put the empty data into tData
      end if
   end if
   return tData
end handler

private handler _decodeUtf8(in pData as Data) returns String
   variable tStr as String
   variable tOk as Boolean
   put "" into tStr
   if the number of bytes in pData is 0 then
      return ""
   end if
   unsafe
      put MCStringDecode(pData, kEncodingUtf8, false, tStr) into tOk
   end unsafe
   if tOk then
      return tStr
   end if
   return ""
end handler

-- The raw bytes of one text field (headers, error, URL ...).
private handler _textData(in pReq as Integer, in pField as Integer) returns Data
   variable tCount as Integer
   _ensureScratch(kScratchCap)
   unsafe
      put _cux_text(pReq, pField, sScratchPtr, sScratchCap) into tCount
   end unsafe
   if tCount < 0 - kScratchCap then
      _ensureScratch(0 - tCount)
      unsafe
         put _cux_text(pReq, pField, sScratchPtr, sScratchCap) into tCount
      end unsafe
   end if
   if tCount <= 0 then
      return the empty data
   end if
   return _bufToData(sScratchPtr, tCount)
end handler

-- Option names to ids. 0 = not a known name (the shim then refuses it and
-- says so in cuLastError). Integer options are below 100, text above.
private handler _optionId(in pName as String) returns Integer
   if pName is "timeout" then
      return kOptTimeoutMs
   else if pName is "connectTimeout" then
      return kOptConnectTimeoutMs
   else if pName is "followRedirects" then
      return kOptFollowRedirects
   else if pName is "maxRedirects" then
      return kOptMaxRedirects
   else if pName is "verifyPeer" then
      return kOptVerifyPeer
   else if pName is "verifyHost" then
      return kOptVerifyHost
   else if pName is "lowSpeedLimit" then
      return kOptLowSpeedLimit
   else if pName is "lowSpeedTime" then
      return kOptLowSpeedTime
   else if pName is "useSsl" then
      return kOptUseSsl
   else if pName is "ftpPassive" then
      return kOptFtpPassive
   else if pName is "maxBodyBytes" then
      return kOptMaxBodyBytes
   else if pName is "httpVersion" then
      return kOptHttpVersion
   else if pName is "dnsCacheSeconds" then
      return kOptDnsCacheSeconds
   else if pName is "createDirs" then
      return kOptCreateDirs
   else if pName is "wsCloseTimeout" then
      return kOptWsCloseTimeoutMs
   else if pName is "username" then
      return kOptUsername
   else if pName is "password" then
      return kOptPassword
   else if pName is "proxy" then
      return kOptProxy
   else if pName is "caFile" then
      return kOptCaFile
   else if pName is "outputFile" then
      return kOptOutputFile
   else if pName is "inputFile" then
      return kOptInputFile
   else if pName is "mailFrom" then
      return kOptMailFrom
   else if pName is "mailRcpt" then
      return kOptMailRcpt
   else if pName is "userAgent" then
      return kOptUserAgent
   else if pName is "sshPublicKey" then
      return kOptSshPublicKey
   else if pName is "sshPrivateKey" then
      return kOptSshPrivateKey
   else if pName is "keyPassword" then
      return kOptKeyPassword
   else if pName is "quote" then
      return kOptQuote
   else if pName is "postQuote" then
      return kOptPostQuote
   else if pName is "proxyUserPassword" then
      return kOptProxyUserpwd
   else if pName is "referer" then
      return kOptReferer
   else if pName is "acceptEncoding" then
      return kOptAcceptEncoding
   end if
   return 0
end handler

private handler _infoId(in pName as String) returns Integer
   if pName is "state" then
      return kInfoState
   else if pName is "result" then
      return kInfoResult
   else if pName is "responseCode" then
      return kInfoResponseCode
   else if pName is "bytesDown" then
      return kInfoBytesDown
   else if pName is "bytesUp" then
      return kInfoBytesUp
   else if pName is "lengthDown" then
      return kInfoLengthDown
   else if pName is "lengthUp" then
      return kInfoLengthUp
   else if pName is "totalTime" then
      return kInfoTotalTime
   else if pName is "redirectCount" then
      return kInfoRedirectCount
   else if pName is "bodySize" then
      return kInfoBodySize
   else if pName is "cancelled" then
      return kInfoCancelled
   else if pName is "wsState" then
      return kInfoWsState
   else if pName is "wsMessages" then
      return kInfoWsMessages
   else if pName is "wsNextType" then
      return kInfoWsNextType
   else if pName is "wsNextSize" then
      return kInfoWsNextSize
   else if pName is "wsCloseCode" then
      return kInfoWsCloseCode
   else if pName is "wsQueuedBytes" then
      return kInfoWsQueuedBytes
   else if pName is "wsPongs" then
      return kInfoWsPongs
   end if
   return 0
end handler

private handler _textId(in pName as String) returns Integer
   if pName is "headers" then
      return kTextHeaders
   else if pName is "error" then
      return kTextError
   else if pName is "effectiveUrl" then
      return kTextEffectiveUrl
   else if pName is "contentType" then
      return kTextContentType
   else if pName is "method" then
      return kTextMethod
   else if pName is "wsCloseReason" then
      return kTextWsCloseReason
   end if
   return 0
end handler

-- ===================================================================== --
--  Public API: lifecycle & diagnostics
-- ===================================================================== --

/**
Summary: Initialize curlxt before any other call.

Returns: The number of holds now taken (1 or more), or a negative error.

Example:
if cuInitialize() < 1 then answer "curlxt failed:" && cuLastError()

Description:
Use <cuInitialize> once at startup, before making a request. It checks
that the installed native library matches this binding and throws an
error if it does not. Calls are counted: each <cuInitialize> needs one
matching <cuCleanup>.

References: cuCleanup (handler), cuLastError (handler)
*/
public handler cuInitialize() returns Integer
   variable tR as Integer
   _checkABI()
   unsafe
      put _cux_init() into tR
   end unsafe
   return tR
end handler

/**
Summary: Give back one hold taken by <cuInitialize>.

Returns: The number of holds still taken; 0 means curlxt is shut down.

Description:
Use <cuCleanup> once for each <cuInitialize>, at quit. The call that
gives back the last hold stops every request still running and frees
every handle, so a stack should give back only the holds it took.

References: cuInitialize (handler)
*/
public handler cuCleanup() returns Integer
   variable tR as Integer
   unsafe
      put _cux_cleanup() into tR
   end unsafe
   return tR
end handler

/**
Summary: The versions of curlxt's ABI, libcurl and the libraries it uses.

Returns: A line such as "curlxt ABI 2; libcurl/8.22.0 OpenSSL/3.5.9 libssh2/1.11.1".

References: cuInitialize (handler)
*/
public handler cuLibraryVersion() returns String
   variable tCount as Integer
   _ensureScratch(kScratchCap)
   unsafe
      put _cux_version_string(sScratchPtr, sScratchCap) into tCount
   end unsafe
   if tCount <= 0 then
      return ""
   end if
   return _decodeUtf8(_bufToData(sScratchPtr, tCount))
end handler

/**
Summary: The last error curlxt recorded, as text.

Returns: The text of the last error, or empty.

Description:
A handler that fails returns 0 or a negative number and records why here.
The error of one finished request is its own: read it with
<cuText>(tRequest, "error").

References: cuClearError (handler), cuText (handler)
*/
public handler cuLastError() returns String
   variable tCount as Integer
   _ensureScratch(kScratchCap)
   unsafe
      put _cux_last_error(sScratchPtr, sScratchCap) into tCount
   end unsafe
   if tCount < 0 - kScratchCap then
      _ensureScratch(0 - tCount)
      unsafe
         put _cux_last_error(sScratchPtr, sScratchCap) into tCount
      end unsafe
   end if
   if tCount <= 0 then
      return ""
   end if
   return _decodeUtf8(_bufToData(sScratchPtr, tCount))
end handler

/**
Summary: Clear the text <cuLastError> returns.

References: cuLastError (handler)
*/
public handler cuClearError()
   unsafe
      _cux_clear_error()
   end unsafe
end handler

-- ===================================================================== --
--  Public API: requests
-- ===================================================================== --

/**
Summary: Make a new request.

pMethod: GET, HEAD, POST, PUT, DELETE, or any other method name. PUT (or
UPLOAD) sends the body as an upload, which is how FTP and SFTP files are
stored and how SMTP sends a message.
pURL: The URL, such as https://example.com/ or sftp://host/path/file.

Returns: A request handle, or 0 if it could not be made (see <cuLastError>).

Example:
put cuRequestNew("GET", "https://example.com/") into tRequest

Description:
The request does nothing until <cuStart>. Before that, set its headers
with <cuSetHeader>, its options with <cuSetOption>, and its body with
<cuSetBody>.

References: cuStart (handler), cuFree (handler), cuSetOption (handler)
*/
public handler cuRequestNew(in pMethod as String, in pURL as String) returns Integer
   variable tR as Integer
   unsafe
      put _cux_request_new(pMethod, pURL) into tR
   end unsafe
   return tR
end handler

/**
Summary: Add one request header.

pRequest: A handle from <cuRequestNew>.
pLine: One header line, such as "Accept: application/json".

Returns: 0, or a negative error.

References: cuRequestNew (handler)
*/
public handler cuSetHeader(in pRequest as Integer, in pLine as String) returns Integer
   variable tR as Integer
   unsafe
      put _cux_set_header(pRequest, pLine) into tR
   end unsafe
   return tR
end handler

/**
Summary: Set a number option of a request.

pRequest: A handle from <cuRequestNew>.
pName: timeout (ms, whole transfer), connectTimeout (ms), followRedirects
(0 or 1), maxRedirects, verifyPeer (0 or 1), verifyHost (0 or 1),
lowSpeedLimit (bytes a second), lowSpeedTime (seconds), useSsl (0 none,
1 try, 2 control, 3 all), ftpPassive (0 or 1), maxBodyBytes (0 = no cap),
httpVersion (0 default, 1 is 1.0, 2 is 1.1), dnsCacheSeconds, createDirs
(0 or 1), wsCloseTimeout (ms a WebSocket waits for the other side to
answer a close; 5000 unless set, 0 = no limit).
pValue: The value.

Returns: 0, or a negative error (an unknown name included).

References: cuSetTextOption (handler)
*/
public handler cuSetOption(in pRequest as Integer, in pName as String, in pValue as Integer) returns Integer
   variable tR as Integer
   variable tId as Integer
   put _optionId(pName) into tId
   if tId > 100 then
      put 0 into tId
   end if
   unsafe
      put _cux_set_int(pRequest, tId, pValue) into tR
   end unsafe
   return tR
end handler

/**
Summary: Set a text option of a request.

pRequest: A handle from <cuRequestNew>.
pName: username, password, proxy, caFile, outputFile (download straight to
this file), inputFile (upload straight from this file), mailFrom,
mailRcpt (adds one recipient), userAgent, sshPublicKey, sshPrivateKey,
keyPassword, quote and postQuote (each adds one FTP or SFTP command, run
before or after the transfer), proxyUserPassword, referer, acceptEncoding.
pValue: The value.

Returns: 0, or a negative error (an unknown name included).

References: cuSetOption (handler)
*/
public handler cuSetTextOption(in pRequest as Integer, in pName as String, in pValue as String) returns Integer
   variable tR as Integer
   variable tId as Integer
   put _optionId(pName) into tId
   if tId < 100 then
      put 0 into tId
   end if
   unsafe
      put _cux_set_text(pRequest, tId, pValue) into tR
   end unsafe
   return tR
end handler

/**
Summary: Set the body a request sends.

pRequest: A handle from <cuRequestNew>.
pData: The bytes to send: the POST body, the PUT or upload content, or a
whole mail message for SMTP.

Returns: 0, or a negative error.

References: cuRequestNew (handler)
*/
public handler cuSetBody(in pRequest as Integer, in pData as Data) returns Integer
   variable tR as Integer
   variable tPtr as Pointer
   variable tLen as Integer
   put the number of bytes in pData into tLen
   if tLen is 0 then
      _ensureScratch(kScratchCap)
      unsafe
         put _cux_set_body(pRequest, sScratchPtr, 0) into tR
      end unsafe
      return tR
   end if
   unsafe
      put MCDataGetBytePtr(pData) into tPtr
      put _cux_set_body(pRequest, tPtr, tLen) into tR
   end unsafe
   return tR
end handler

/**
Summary: Start a request.

pRequest: A handle from <cuRequestNew>.

Returns: 0, or a negative error (an output or input file that cannot be
opened is refused here).

Description:
A started request runs while <cuPoll> or <cuWait> is called. After
<cuStart> its options can no longer change.

References: cuPoll (handler), cuWait (handler)
*/
public handler cuStart(in pRequest as Integer) returns Integer
   variable tR as Integer
   unsafe
      put _cux_start(pRequest) into tR
   end unsafe
   return tR
end handler

/**
Summary: Stop a request.

pRequest: A handle from <cuRequestNew>.

Returns: 0, or a negative error.

Description:
A cancelled request is reported by <cuPoll> like any other that ended,
with result 1000, so a callback waiting on it still arrives. Cancelling a
finished request does nothing.

References: cuStart (handler)
*/
public handler cuCancel(in pRequest as Integer) returns Integer
   variable tR as Integer
   unsafe
      put _cux_cancel(pRequest) into tR
   end unsafe
   return tR
end handler

/**
Summary: Release a request and everything it holds.

pRequest: A handle from <cuRequestNew>.

Returns: 0, or a negative error. After this the handle is stale.

References: cuRequestNew (handler)
*/
public handler cuFree(in pRequest as Integer) returns Integer
   variable tR as Integer
   unsafe
      put _cux_free(pRequest) into tR
   end unsafe
   return tR
end handler

/**
Summary: Move every running request along, and list those that ended.

Returns: A comma-separated list of the request handles that have ended
since the last call, or empty. Each is listed once.

Description:
Call <cuPoll> on a timer for as long as requests run in the background:
nothing moves between calls. 20 to 50 milliseconds is a good interval.
The curlHelpers library does this for you.

References: cuWait (handler), cuStart (handler)
*/
public handler cuPoll() returns String
   variable tCount as Integer
   _ensureScratch(kScratchCap)
   unsafe
      put _cux_poll(sScratchPtr, sScratchCap) into tCount
   end unsafe
   if tCount < 0 - kScratchCap then
      _ensureScratch(0 - tCount)
      unsafe
         put _cux_poll(sScratchPtr, sScratchCap) into tCount
      end unsafe
   end if
   if tCount <= 0 then
      return ""
   end if
   return _decodeUtf8(_bufToData(sScratchPtr, tCount))
end handler

/**
Summary: Wait for one request to end.

pRequest: A started request.
pTimeoutMs: The longest to wait, in milliseconds; -1 waits for the
request's own timeouts alone.

Returns: 1 when it ended, 0 when the wait ran out (it keeps running, and
<cuPoll> reports it later), or a negative error.

Description:
The script pauses while it waits. Other running requests move too.

References: cuPoll (handler)
*/
public handler cuWait(in pRequest as Integer, in pTimeoutMs as Integer) returns Integer
   variable tR as Integer
   unsafe
      put _cux_wait(pRequest, pTimeoutMs) into tR
   end unsafe
   return tR
end handler

/**
Summary: A number about a request.

pRequest: A request handle.
pName: state (0 new, 1 running, 2 ended), result (0 = success, a libcurl
error number, 1000 = cancelled, -1 while running), responseCode, bytesDown,
bytesUp, lengthDown and lengthUp (-1 = not known), totalTime (seconds),
redirectCount, bodySize, cancelled (0 or 1). For a WebSocket also wsState
(1 connecting, 2 open, 3 closing, 4 closed; 0 = not a WebSocket),
wsMessages (messages waiting to be read), wsNextType (1 text, 2 binary,
0 = none waiting), wsNextSize (bytes), wsCloseCode, wsQueuedBytes (sent
by script, not yet on the wire), wsPongs (pongs received).

Returns: The number, or -1 for a stale handle or an unknown name.

References: cuText (handler)
*/
public handler cuInfo(in pRequest as Integer, in pName as String) returns Number
   variable tR as Number
   unsafe
      put _cux_info(pRequest, _infoId(pName)) into tR
   end unsafe
   return tR
end handler

/**
Summary: A piece of text about a request.

pRequest: A request handle.
pName: headers (the final response's header block), error, effectiveUrl,
contentType, method, wsCloseReason (the reason a WebSocket's close gave).

Returns: The text, decoded from UTF-8, or empty.

References: cuTextData (handler), cuInfo (handler)
*/
public handler cuText(in pRequest as Integer, in pName as String) returns String
   return _decodeUtf8(_textData(pRequest, _textId(pName)))
end handler

/**
Summary: A piece of text about a request, as its raw bytes.

pRequest: A handle from <cuRequestNew>.

pName: The field name, as for <cuText>.

Description:
Use <cuTextData> instead of <cuText> where a server may send headers that
are not UTF-8.

References: cuText (handler)
*/
public handler cuTextData(in pRequest as Integer, in pName as String) returns Data
   return _textData(pRequest, _textId(pName))
end handler

/**
Summary: The response body a request received.

pRequest: A handle from <cuRequestNew>.

Returns: The bytes, or empty. Reading the body does not release it;
<cuFree> does. A request with an outputFile holds no body.

References: cuFree (handler), cuInfo (handler)
*/
public handler cuBody(in pRequest as Integer) returns Data
   variable tSize as Number
   variable tCount as Integer
   variable tPtr as Pointer
   variable tOk as Boolean
   variable tData as Data
   unsafe
      put _cux_info(pRequest, kInfoBodySize) into tSize
   end unsafe
   if tSize <= 0 then
      return the empty data
   end if
   -- A block of its own, freed before returning: a body can be large, and
   -- growing the shared scratch buffer to it would hold that memory for the
   -- life of the process.
   put false into tOk
   unsafe
      put MCMemoryAllocate(tSize, tPtr) into tOk
   end unsafe
   if not tOk then
      throw "curlxt: failed to allocate a buffer for the response body."
   end if
   unsafe
      put _cux_body(pRequest, tPtr, tSize) into tCount
   end unsafe
   put _bufToData(tPtr, tCount) into tData
   unsafe
      MCMemoryDeallocate(tPtr)
   end unsafe
   return tData
end handler

/**
Summary: How many request handles are live.

Returns: The count of requests made and not yet freed.

References: cuFree (handler)
*/
public handler cuLiveCount() returns Integer
   variable tR as Integer
   unsafe
      put _cux_live_count() into tR
   end unsafe
   return tR
end handler

-- ===================================================================== --
--  Public API: WebSockets (ABI 2). Ran on OXT-Beyond's headless Linux
--  server engine 2026-11-21 (tests/engine-selftest.lc, ws:// and wss://);
--  the IDE and the other platforms need an OXT pass.
-- ===================================================================== --

-- One message out: the bytes of pData as a frame of kind pKind.
private handler _wsSend(in pSocket as Integer, in pKind as Integer, in pData as Data) returns Integer
   variable tR as Integer
   variable tPtr as Pointer
   variable tLen as Integer
   put the number of bytes in pData into tLen
   if tLen is 0 then
      _ensureScratch(kScratchCap)
      unsafe
         put _cux_ws_send(pSocket, pKind, sScratchPtr, 0) into tR
      end unsafe
      return tR
   end if
   unsafe
      put MCDataGetBytePtr(pData) into tPtr
      put _cux_ws_send(pSocket, pKind, tPtr, tLen) into tR
   end unsafe
   return tR
end handler

/**
Summary: Make a new WebSocket.

pURL: The address, starting with ws:// or wss:// (wss is the secure kind).

Returns: A socket handle, or 0 if it could not be made (see <cuLastError>).

Example:
put cuWsNew("wss://example.com/chat") into tSocket
get cuSetHeader(tSocket, "Sec-WebSocket-Protocol: chat")
get cuStart(tSocket)

Description:
A WebSocket is a request handle: set its headers with <cuSetHeader> and
its options with <cuSetOption> and <cuSetTextOption> (caFile, proxy,
verifyPeer, connectTimeout and the rest apply), then start it with
<cuStart>. The timeout option is the longest the connection may take to
open; it does not limit how long the socket then stays open. It connects
while <cuWsPoll> or <cuPoll> is called, or under <cuWsWait>. Ask
<cuInfo>(tSocket, "wsState") where it is: 1 connecting, 2 open,
3 closing, 4 closed. Release it with <cuFree>.

<cuPoll> never lists a WebSocket.

References: cuStart (handler), cuWsSendText (handler), cuWsRead (handler), cuWsClose (handler), cuWsPoll (handler), cuFree (handler)
*/
public handler cuWsNew(in pURL as String) returns Integer
   variable tR as Integer
   unsafe
      put _cux_ws_new(pURL) into tR
   end unsafe
   return tR
end handler

/**
Summary: Send a text message on a WebSocket.

pSocket: An open socket from <cuWsNew>.
pText: The text. It is sent as UTF-8.

Returns: 0, or a negative error: -4 when the socket is not open, or when
the other side has stopped reading and too much is already waiting.

Description:
The whole message is taken at once. What the network does not accept
straight away goes out as <cuWsPoll> runs; <cuInfo>(pSocket,
"wsQueuedBytes") says how much is still waiting.

References: cuWsSendData (handler), cuWsReadText (handler)
*/
public handler cuWsSendText(in pSocket as Integer, in pText as String) returns Integer
   variable tData as Data
   variable tOk as Boolean
   put the empty data into tData
   put false into tOk
   unsafe
      put MCStringEncode(pText, kEncodingUtf8, false, tData) into tOk
   end unsafe
   if not tOk then
      return -3
   end if
   return _wsSend(pSocket, kWsKindText, tData)
end handler

/**
Summary: Send a binary message on a WebSocket.

pSocket: An open socket from <cuWsNew>.
pData: The bytes.

Returns: 0, or a negative error, as for <cuWsSendText>.

References: cuWsSendText (handler), cuWsRead (handler)
*/
public handler cuWsSendData(in pSocket as Integer, in pData as Data) returns Integer
   return _wsSend(pSocket, kWsKindBinary, pData)
end handler

/**
Summary: Send a ping on a WebSocket, to check the other side is there.

pSocket: An open socket from <cuWsNew>.
pData: Up to 125 bytes to send with it, or empty.

Returns: 0, or a negative error.

Description:
The other side answers a ping with a pong. <cuInfo>(pSocket, "wsPongs")
counts the pongs received. Pings FROM the other side are answered for
you.

References: cuWsNew (handler), cuInfo (handler)
*/
public handler cuWsPing(in pSocket as Integer, in pData as Data) returns Integer
   return _wsSend(pSocket, kWsKindPing, pData)
end handler

/**
Summary: Close a WebSocket politely.

pSocket: A socket from <cuWsNew>.
pCode: The close code: 1000 for a normal close, 1001, a code of your own
from 3000 to 4999, or 0 for none.
pReason: A short reason (up to 123 bytes), or empty.

Returns: 0, or a negative error.

Description:
The socket tells the other side it is closing (wsState 3) and is closed
(wsState 4) when the other side answers, or when the wsCloseTimeout
option runs out. Messages that arrive meanwhile can still be read.
Closing a closed socket does nothing. To drop a socket at once, without
telling the other side, use <cuCancel>.

References: cuWsNew (handler), cuCancel (handler), cuFree (handler)
*/
public handler cuWsClose(in pSocket as Integer, in pCode as Integer, in pReason as String) returns Integer
   variable tR as Integer
   unsafe
      put _cux_ws_close(pSocket, pCode, pReason) into tR
   end unsafe
   return tR
end handler

/**
Summary: Take the next message a WebSocket received, as bytes.

pSocket: A socket from <cuWsNew>.

Returns: The bytes of the oldest waiting message, or empty.

Description:
A message can itself be empty, so ask <cuInfo>(pSocket, "wsMessages")
how many are waiting before reading, and <cuInfo>(pSocket, "wsNextType")
whether the next one is text (1) or binary (2). A message split into
pieces on the way arrives here whole. Messages that arrived before a
socket closed can be read after it.

References: cuWsReadText (handler), cuWsPoll (handler), cuInfo (handler)
*/
public handler cuWsRead(in pSocket as Integer) returns Data
   variable tSize as Number
   variable tWaiting as Number
   variable tCount as Integer
   variable tPtr as Pointer
   variable tOk as Boolean
   variable tData as Data
   unsafe
      put _cux_info(pSocket, kInfoWsMessages) into tWaiting
      put _cux_info(pSocket, kInfoWsNextSize) into tSize
   end unsafe
   if tWaiting < 1 then
      return the empty data
   end if
   if tSize < 1 then
      -- an empty message: take it off the queue
      _ensureScratch(kScratchCap)
      unsafe
         put _cux_ws_read(pSocket, sScratchPtr, sScratchCap) into tCount
      end unsafe
      return the empty data
   end if
   -- A block of its own, freed before returning (as cuBody does).
   put false into tOk
   unsafe
      put MCMemoryAllocate(tSize, tPtr) into tOk
   end unsafe
   if not tOk then
      throw "curlxt: failed to allocate a buffer for the WebSocket message."
   end if
   unsafe
      put _cux_ws_read(pSocket, tPtr, tSize) into tCount
   end unsafe
   put _bufToData(tPtr, tCount) into tData
   unsafe
      MCMemoryDeallocate(tPtr)
   end unsafe
   return tData
end handler

/**
Summary: Take the next message a WebSocket received, as text.

pSocket: A socket from <cuWsNew>.

Returns: The oldest waiting message, decoded from UTF-8, or empty.

Description:
Use it for text messages (wsNextType 1); read a binary one with
<cuWsRead>.

References: cuWsRead (handler), cuWsSendText (handler)
*/
public handler cuWsReadText(in pSocket as Integer) returns String
   return _decodeUtf8(cuWsRead(pSocket))
end handler

/**
Summary: Move every WebSocket (and every request) along.

Returns: How many received messages are waiting to be read, over every
socket, or a negative error.

Description:
Call <cuWsPoll> on a timer while a socket is in use: nothing is sent or
received between calls. Unlike <cuPoll> it reports no finished requests
and takes none off <cuPoll>'s list, so it is safe to call beside the
curlHelpers or tsNet libraries. The curlHelpers library (cuWsOpen) runs
the timer for you.

References: cuPoll (handler), cuWsWait (handler)
*/
public handler cuWsPoll() returns Integer
   variable tR as Integer
   unsafe
      put _cux_ws_poll() into tR
   end unsafe
   return tR
end handler

/**
Summary: Wait until something happens on a WebSocket.

pSocket: A started socket from <cuWsNew>.
pTimeoutMs: The longest to wait, in milliseconds; -1 waits without limit.

Returns: 1 when a message is waiting, the socket has closed, or a
connecting socket has opened; 0 when the wait ran out; or a negative
error.

Description:
The script pauses while it waits. Other sockets and requests move too.

It answers 1 at once, and moves nothing, while a message is already
waiting to be read. To wait for something that comes after those
messages, such as the socket closing, read them first with <cuWsRead> or
<cuWsReadText>, or call <cuWsPoll> in a loop instead.

References: cuWsPoll (handler), cuWsRead (handler), cuWsReadText (handler)
*/
public handler cuWsWait(in pSocket as Integer, in pTimeoutMs as Integer) returns Integer
   variable tR as Integer
   unsafe
      put _cux_ws_wait(pSocket, pTimeoutMs) into tR
   end unsafe
   return tR
end handler

end library
